        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your 81-year-old female patient, who presented with an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she exhibited significant dyspnoea, increased sputum production, and reduced oxygen saturation. A chest X-ray confirmed pulmonary hyperinflation consistent with COPD without signs of pneumonia. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Blood tests showed mild inflammatory markers. She was promptly initiated on supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. Vital signs were closely monitored throughout her stay. She responded well to treatment with clear clinical improvement. At discharge, she is stable, ambulatory, and has received thorough education regarding her medication regimen and when to seek further medical attention. Please arrange follow-up within two weeks. Kind regards.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
